From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mac80211: fix the removal of a non-MLD AP_VLAN

Fix two problems when hostapd removes a dynamic VLAN (AP_VLAN)
interface:

- "mtk: mac80211: remove links when removing AP_VLAN interface" also
  clears link 0, the deflink, of a non-MLD AP_VLAN. Its group keys then
  can't be unlinked (-ENOLINK) but are freed anyway, and
  ieee80211_teardown_sdata() crashes on the stale key list. Only clear
  the links of an MLD AP_VLAN.

- With the deflink kept, ieee80211_do_stop() releases the AP_VLAN's
  copy of the AP's channel context through the driver, which warns
  "Failed check-sdata-in-driver check". Restore the upstream AP_VLAN
  check in ieee80211_link_release_channel(), which the revert of
  "Create separate links for VLAN interfaces" removed.

--- a/net/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -5608,6 +5608,16 @@
 	if (wdev->iftype == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) {
 		int i;
 
+		/*
+		 * Only an AP_VLAN of an MLD AP shares the AP's links. A
+		 * non-MLD AP_VLAN uses its deflink as link 0, and its group
+		 * keys use link ID 0; clearing it would make
+		 * ieee80211_key_replace() fail with -ENOLINK while the keys
+		 * are freed, leaving freed keys on the key list.
+		 */
+		if (!ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif))
+			return;
+
 		sdata->vif.valid_links = 0;
 		sdata->vif.active_links = 0;
 		sdata->vif.dormant_links = 0;
--- a/net/mac80211/chan.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/chan.c
@@ -2267,6 +2267,9 @@ void ieee80211_link_release_channel(struct ieee80211_link_data *link)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata = link->sdata;
 
+	if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
+		return;
+
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(sdata->local->hw.wiphy);
 
 	if (rcu_access_pointer(link->conf->chanctx_conf))
